				},
				{
					"id": "tq4Z3RDMZOaeJ7FL4",
					"name": "Necrodermis (Flayed One)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 50, all locations. Weak Points 4 (a Warrior-tier chassis, per framework.md): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 4 or less halves DR (25). Eye-slit optics run at DR 25 rather than 50.\n\nLore: Necrodermis is a Necron's body and its armour at once: a skin of near-indestructible living metal with no separate suit to strip away. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Necron fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that necrodermis is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Necron anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Necrons"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 50,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 50
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "Thk0_saKG1ify06r7",
			"name": "Mind: Flayer Curse",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Flayer Curse is a degeneration of a Necron's reanimation matrix that erases whatever personality survived the biotransference and replaces it with a single, murderous compulsion.\n\nDesign: -10 (Bloodlust) - 15 (Compulsive Behavior) - 10 (Social Stigma) = -35 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tBQsgLB0m9dYfDGws",
					"name": "Bloodlust",
					"reference": "B125",
					"local_notes": "As Bloodlust, but specifically the compulsion to flay and take the flesh of a defeated foe.\n\nLore: The Flayer Curse turns a Necron's reanimation-matrix corruption into a compulsion to kill and flay, over and over -- Codex background's core description of Flayed Ones.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Bloodlust (B125), self-control 12, -10 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Necrons"
					],
					"base_points": -10,
					"cr": 12
				},
				{
					"id": "taoW6Y3w6S75kbMlY",
					"name": "Compulsive Behavior (Flesh-Taking)",
					"reference": "B128",
					"local_notes": "Must wear or carry flayed skin taken personally; goes without it only under duress, and poorly.\n\nLore: Flayed Ones are consistently shown draped in the skins of their victims, a compulsion rather than a fashion choice.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Compulsive Behavior (B128), self-control 12, -15 points (Serious tier, since it is the caste's whole defining trait).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Necrons"
					],
					"base_points": -15,
					"cr": 12
				},
				{
					"id": "trU0iG32F-hcmBQMy",
					"name": "Social Stigma (Cursed Outcast)",
					"reference": "B155",
					"local_notes": "Shunned and quarantined by other Necrons, including their own dynasty, as a contamination risk.\n\nLore: Even other Necrons keep Flayed Ones at arm's length, Codex background treating the Flayer Curse as a contagion-like degeneration rather than a lifestyle choice.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Social Stigma (B155), -10 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Xenos",
						"Necrons"
					],
					"base_points": -10
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sWUON7SqEvdSvr7aH",
			"name": "Brawling",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Flayed One's built-in bladed claws are its whole reason for closing to melee at all.\n\nDesign: Brawling (DX/E), the skill the Flayed One Claws weapon line uses. DX+3 (15) for 8 points, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "sh36uc7kASCpc5ZAn",
			"name": "Stealth",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Flayed One stalks a victim for as long as it takes, unseen.\n\nDesign: DX+2 (14) for 8 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "sGqr5p3rJKNPIO8TX",
			"name": "Climbing",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Flayed Ones are consistently described dropping on prey from above, out of ducts, rafters or ruined upper floors.\n\nDesign: DX+0 (12) for 2 points, Average.",
